  "strategy": "**Approach and Rationale**  \n  We develop a genetic algorithm (GA) with simulated binary crossover (SBX) and polynomial mutation to find a solution with a lower C5 bound. This approach explores a broader solution space than local search, leveraging diversity to escape local optima. The algorithm includes constraints enforcement via repair mechanisms and evaluates candidates using cross-correlation. We hypothesize this yields a lower bound than local optimization alone.\n  \n  **Mathematical Specification**  \n  - **Representation**: A 70-point solution vector \\(h \\in [0, 1]^{70}\\) with \\(\\sum h = 35\\).\n  - **Objective**: Minimize \\(C_5 = \\max_k \\int h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx\\).\n  - **Constraints**: \\(0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1\\), \\(\\sum h = 35\\).\n  - **Repair**: Adjust sums and clip values to [0, 1] using iterative adjustment.\n  - **Crossover/Mutation**: SBX and polynomial mutation with parameters \\(\\eta = 20\\), mutation probability 0.1.\n\n  **Implementation Procedure**  \n  1. **Initialization**:  \n     - Population size: 200.  \n     - Include provided parent if available; otherwise, initialize randomly.  \n   2. **Fitness Evaluation**:  \n     - Compute \\(compute_c5(h)\\) for each candidate after repair.  \n   3. **Selection**: Tournament selection with size 3.  \n   4. **Crossover**: SBX with \\(\\eta = 20\\).  \n   5. **Mutation**: Polynomial mutation with \\(\\eta = 20\\).  \n   6. **Repair**: Iterative adjustment to satisfy sum = 35 and clip to [0, 1].  \n   7. **Termination**: 55 generations or time limit (1100 seconds).  \n\n  **Search Choices and Variations**  \n  - Use 70-point samples.  \n  - Repair if sum not met during initialization.  \n  - SBX crossover and polynomial mutation.  \n  - Tournament size 3.  \n\n  **Computation Budget and Robustness**  \n  - Per-generations time: ~1.2 seconds (est.).  \n  - Max generations: 55 (budget ~660 seconds).  \n  - Handle repair failures by restarting mutation.  \n  - Fallback: Return best from initialized population.  \n\n  **Validation and Return Contract**  \n  - Ensure \\(0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1\\), \\(\\sum h = 35\\).  \n  - Return best solution and \\(C_5\\).  \n  - Maximum \\(C_5\\): 0.38085.",
